    "turn_text": "us in... I agree 100%. I agree 100%. Thank you for the call. I think that the people who are doing the water throwing are frigging idiots. You know what I'm saying? Mouth breathers are the first rank. And I believe that there is blood on the hands of those who advance themselves by running down police. They are promoters of bigotry. Some of them, they get some prominence out of it politically. Some of them, they build themselves up, they get votes, they get a grant. You know, if you complain about the city police department is terrible, terrible after a while, the city gives you a grant. That's either to solve the problem or to shut you up, but either way, you know, you get the money and you stop talking. So there are folks, and also it's like any sort of bigotry. There are people who become impassioned and in love with the hatred that's in their hearts. And just so we're clear, hating somebody because of what they do for a living is morally the same as hating somebody because of the color of their skin or their orientation or their religion or anything else along those lines. It's all bigotry and it's all wrong. But words have consequences. And when you have an entire society, look at so many of our big entertainers. Look at the people on the evening news. Look at the friggin governor of this day. People who trashed the police in law enforcement on an ongoing and regular basis. Do they think those words just go out into space? No, they go into the minds of people, and it is a fertilizer of hatred on the worst deeds and impulses of those people. And it leads to situations like this, and sadly, a whole heck of a lot worse. Bill, glad you called, sir. Welcome to 570WSIR. Hi, Bob.",
