    "turn_text": "Well, you know what I saw is a logistical crisis that is truly humanitarian and its nature. I mean, you got systems that are designed down there, facilities designed down there for, you know, 2,000 people that are trying to handle, you know, 10,000 people. And what you see is the border agents doing yeoman's work uh... humane uh... treatment of that crisis and uh... with the tool that are available to them and i'll just tell you the folks that are down there using it for political uh... fodder and just partisan politics is despicable uh... they're doing the best they can these border guards are are heroes they should not be insulted they not shoot they should not be chastised and to say america is the blame for this is just appalling to make",
